ATTRIBUTION

Apache-2.0 section 4 asks you to retain this file and to state any
changes you made. If you use Safegate, credit:

    Safegate
    https://github.com/decrypto-official/decrypto-safegate

If you modified the pattern dictionary or the registry, please say so
plainly. Someone reading a score needs to know whose dictionary and whose
registry produced it, because those two directories are what a score
actually means. A score computed against a modified registry is not
comparable to one computed against this repository's registry, and
presenting it as such would mislead the reader.

Sharing improvements back is not required. It is the whole reason this is
public, and a pull request helps everyone downstream of you.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

THIS IS NOT FINANCIAL ADVICE, AND IT IS NOT A SAFETY RATING.

Safegate reports the structural capabilities present in a token's deployed
code, with an explicit measure of how much it was able to check. It does
not predict behaviour, it cannot observe off-chain risk, and it never
certifies any token as safe.

Read LIMITATIONS.md before relying on any output. If you surface Safegate
results to end users, carry the coverage figure and the limitations with
them. A bare score presented as a verdict is a misuse of this project,
whatever the licence permits.
